# Related Fix Rotation Rule

Internal links must be contextually relevant and rotated.

Cursor must NOT output the same 3 related links on every page.

Rules:

1. Related fixes must belong to the same protocol cluster:
   - SPF pages → link to other SPF fixes
   - DKIM pages → link to other DKIM fixes
   - DMARC pages → link to other DMARC fixes

2. Select 3 related pages that are technically relevant to the issue.

3. The same set of links must not appear identically across many pages.

4. Use descriptive anchor text (not raw URLs).

5. Always include ONE link back to the protocol hub:
   - /spf
   - /dkim
   - /dmarc

Goal:
Create a natural internal link graph instead of repetitive patterns.